--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SECURITY MODEL
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

IP Lock (middleware.ts):
  - Kiosk routes (/, /menu, /cart, /payment, /confirmed, /status) are locked to
    KIOSK_IP. Any other device gets 403. Localhost always allowed.
  - Student portal (/student/*) is blocked from the kiosk IP — prevents
    students from opening /student on the kiosk device.

Session Auth:
  - /admin/* — requires iron-session cookie (admin session). Redirects to
    /admin/login if not authenticated.
  - /student/* — requires iron-session cookie (student session). Redirects to
    /student if not authenticated. Forces /student/change-pin if isTemporaryPin.

Kitchen PIN Gate:
  - /kitchen is protected by a staff PIN stored in .env as KITCHEN_PIN.
  - Verified via POST /api/kitchen/auth, which sets an iron-session cookie
    (role: 'kitchen'). Server-side — cannot be faked from browser console.
  - Rate limited: 10 attempts/min per IP.
  - Logout: DELETE /api/kitchen/auth destroys the session cookie.
  - All kitchen API calls (order edits, status changes, cancels, cleanup)
    require a valid kitchen or admin session — enforced server-side on every route.

Queue (/queue):
  - Intentionally open. Read-only, shows order numbers only, no sensitive data.
    Designed to be displayed on a public TV screen.

API-level Guards:
  - Admin APIs (/api/admin/*, /api/menu-items, /api/orders/metrics|stats|logs)
    check admin session cookie — middleware alone is not enough since middleware
    only covers page routes, not /api/*.
  - Kitchen APIs (/api/orders GET+PATCH, /api/orders/cleanup) require kitchen
    or admin session. All order mutations (status, cancel, edit) are gated.
  - Menu-items PATCH whitelists allowed fields (name, price, description, image,
    stock, available, categoryId) — no mass-assignment via raw body.
  - Order creation caps: max 10 distinct items per order, max qty 20 per item.
  - Paid orders cannot be edited — server rejects edit requests if
    paymentStatus === 'paid', regardless of UI state.
  - Cashless pay is atomic (Prisma $transaction) — paymentStatus re-checked
    inside transaction to prevent double-payment race condition.
  - Kiosk cashless PIN brute force: 3 wrong attempts → 30-second lockout per account
    (tracked in StudentAccount.pinAttempts + pinLockedUntil).
  - Student portal login brute force: 5 wrong PINs → 15-minute account lockout
    (same pinAttempts/pinLockedUntil fields). Also: 10 login attempts/min per IP.
  - Cashless identify endpoint: 30 requests/min per IP rate limit.
  - Rate limiter: in-memory (src/lib/rate-limit.ts), resets on server restart.
    Suitable for single-instance local deployment. No Redis needed.
  - Stock is pre-validated on the payment page (fresh fetch) before order
    submission — catches stock changes between cart and checkout.

Password/PIN Storage:
  - All passwords and PINs stored as bcrypt hashes (cost 10). Never stored plain.
  - QR tokens are UUIDs — unguessable, no personal data encoded in the QR.

Two-Factor Narrative (cashless):
  - Physical QR card (something you HAVE) + 4-digit PIN (something you KNOW)
  - If QR card lost/stolen: admin regenerates qrToken → old card dead instantly
  - If PIN compromised: admin resets PIN → student sets new one on next login

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ADMIN ABUSE PREVENTION (TOP-UP ACCOUNTABILITY)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Problem: Any admin with system access can credit arbitrary amounts to student
accounts. This is a financial trust problem present in all cashless reload
systems (GCash reload centers, school canteen cards, prepaid systems).

Technical controls implemented:
  1. Required reference note — every top-up/adjustment requires a text note
     (e.g. "Cash received from student", "Receipt #0012"). Cannot be submitted
     blank — enforced at both UI and API level.
  2. Admin ID logged — every transaction records which admin performed it +
     exact timestamp. Immutable once written.
  3. Top-up Audit Log — dedicated page at Admin → Students → Top-up Audit
     showing all balance adjustments across all students: who did it, when,
     how much, and the reference note. Any admin can view this.

What code cannot prevent:
  An admin can still write a fake note. Technical controls create a paper trail
  and raise the cost of abuse — they do not eliminate the possibility.

Recommended institutional controls (outside the system):
  - Supervisor periodically reviews the Top-up Audit log
  - Physical receipt books: admin writes a receipt per top-up, student signs it
  - Cash reconciliation: total top-ups credited by admin should match cash
    collected and deposited
  - Two-person rule: one admin credits, a different person reviews (if staffing allows)

For the study paper:
  "The system logs all balance adjustments with admin identity, timestamp, and
  a mandatory reference note (enforced at the API level). Institutional oversight
  — cash handling procedures, supervisor review of the audit log, and physical
  receipt documentation — provides the primary accountability layer. This mirrors
  the accountability model used in real-world cashless reload systems."

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PAYMENT FLOWS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Cash:
  Order created (awaiting_payment) → kitchen confirms cash → preparing
  → kitchen marks ready → completed

GCash:
  Order created (pending_verification) → kitchen confirms GCash receipt → preparing
  → kitchen marks ready → completed
  On confirmation: order totalAmount added to GCashAccount.monthlyReceived

Cashless (normal — kiosk QR scan):
  Order created (pending_verification) → kiosk camera scans student QR card
  → student enters PIN → balance deducted atomically → order jumps to preparing
  → kitchen marks ready → completed

Cashless (fallback — cashier manual entry):
  If student cannot use kiosk → kitchen shows "Confirm Cashless" button
  → modal opens → cashier asks student for ID number + PIN → enters both
  → same PIN validation + balance deduction → order moves to preparing
  API: POST /api/cashless/pay-by-id

Cancellation with refunds:
  - Cashless paid orders: cancel auto-refunds balance to student account
    (StudentTransaction type=refund created, refundStatus=completed)
  - GCash paid orders: cancel flags refundStatus=pending — admin handles
    manual GCash reversal separately
  - Unpaid orders: cancel with no money movement

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
TRICKY STUFF WE SOLVED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Route Group Conflict:
  Next.js route groups (parentheses folders) don't add URL segments. Originally
  student portal was (student)/ which conflicted with (kiosk)/ — both resolved
  to /. Fixed by renaming to student/ (a real path segment).

Camera QR Scanning:
  html5-qrcode failed silently on Windows Chrome. BarcodeDetector API is
  Android-only by default on Chrome. Solved by using getUserMedia + jsQR:
  get raw video stream, draw frames to canvas, pass pixel data to jsQR.
  This works on all Chromium browsers (Chrome, Brave, Edge) on any platform.

play() Race Condition:
  Calling video.play() manually after setting srcObject caused
  "play() interrupted by new load request" error in dev mode (React strict mode
  runs effects twice). Fixed by adding autoPlay attribute to <video> and
  removing the manual play() call.

params in Next.js 14 vs 15:
  Next.js 15 made params async (Promise<{id}>), requiring use() or await.
  This project runs Next.js 14 where params is a plain object. use(params)
  throws "unsupported type passed to use()". Fixed by accessing params.id directly.

IP Lock + Localhost:
  Setting KIOSK_IP blocks the server PC from accessing its own kiosk if using
  localhost, because the request IP is 127.0.0.1, not the machine's LAN IP.
  Fixed: middleware always allows 127.0.0.1 and ::1 regardless of KIOSK_IP.

GCash Monthly Limit Idempotency:
  monthlyReceived should only increment once per confirmed payment.
  Guard: only increment when current paymentStatus !== 'paid' AND new
  paymentStatus === 'paid'. Prevents double-counting if PATCH called twice.

Double-Spend Prevention:
  Initial cashless pay did balance check then wrote in two separate DB calls.
  Race condition: concurrent requests could both pass the check with stale balance.
  Fixed with Prisma interactive transaction — fresh paymentStatus AND fresh
  balance re-read inside the transaction before any write. Applies to both
  /api/cashless/pay (QR scan) and /api/cashless/pay-by-id (manual entry).

SQLite WAL Mode:
  Default SQLite journal mode serializes all writes — concurrent kiosk orders
  queue behind each other, risking "database is locked" errors under load.
  Fixed via src/instrumentation.ts (Next.js startup hook): runs
  PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL and PRAGMA busy_timeout=5000 on server start.
  WAL allows concurrent readers + one writer without blocking. Enabled in
  next.config.mjs via experimental.instrumentationHook: true.

Cart Cleared Too Early (GCash/Cashless):
  Payment page called clearCart() immediately after order creation, before payment
  completed. If student went back from GCash or Cashless (insufficient balance),
  cart was empty. Fixed: clearCart() moved to completion point — GCash clears on
  "I've Sent Payment" click, Cashless clears on payment success stage.

Soft Delete for Audit Trail:
  Hard-deleting a student account also deleted all transaction history — admin
  could top up fraudulently then delete the account to erase evidence. Fixed with
  soft delete: "Delete" sets status='deleted', data stays in DB forever. Top-up
  audit log shows transactions from deleted accounts. Balance must be ₱0 before
  deletion is allowed.

Stock Deduction Timing:
  Stock is deducted atomically at order creation (inside the same DB transaction
  as the order insert). This prevents overselling between concurrent kiosks —
  the first POST to commit wins; the second gets a stock error.
  Stock is restored on cancellation at any stage (UI cancel, GCash auto-timeout,
  admin delete of non-completed orders). A floor guard ensures stock never goes
  below 0 due to edge-case bugs. Edit order adjusts stock by delta only.

